IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory): the provision index.
--
-- One entry for every chapter, part, division, schedule, schedule part and section of the text, for the dictionary and its two parts,
-- and for the two tables that other provisions cite, each with its identifier and its heading as the text prints them.
-- The entries are written by a script that reads the text file; none is typed by hand.
-- `first line` and `last line` are line numbers in the deposited text file.
-- The text is the unofficial plain-text rendering deposited with this encoding, not the authorised republication.

§ `Provision index`

DECLARE `Kind of provision` IS ONE OF
    `a chapter`
    `a part`
    `a division`
    `a schedule`
    `a section`
    `a part of the dictionary`
    `the dictionary`
    `a table`

DECLARE `Provision` HAS
    `identifier` IS A STRING
    `kind` IS A `Kind of provision`
    `heading` IS A STRING
    `first line` IS A NUMBER
    `last line` IS A NUMBER
    `in scope` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Provision path` HAS
    `section` IS A STRING
    `path` IS A STRING


GIVETH A LIST OF `Provision`
`the provision index` MEANS
    LIST
        (`Provision` WITH `identifier` IS "Chapter 1", `kind` IS `a chapter`, `heading` IS "Preliminary", `first line` IS 68, `last line` IS 231, `in scope` IS TRUE)
        , (`Provision` WITH `identifier` IS "Part 1.1", `kind` IS `a part`, `heading` IS "General", `first line` IS 70, `last line` IS 149, `in scope` IS TRUE)
