-- The heading of the provision whose identifier is given, as the text prints it; NOTHING if the index has no such provision.
GIVEN id IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the heading of the provision` MEANS `the heading found in` id `the provision index`

GIVEN id IS A STRING, entries IS A LIST OF `Provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the heading found in` MEANS
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   first's `identifier` EQUALS id
        THEN JUST (first's `heading`)
        ELSE `the heading found in` id rest

-- Whether the provision whose identifier is given is in the scope this encoding covers; NOTHING if the index has no such provision.
GIVEN id IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the provision is in scope` MEANS `the scope found in` id `the provision index`

GIVEN id IS A STRING, entries IS A LIST OF `Provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the scope found in` MEANS
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   first's `identifier` EQUALS id
        THEN JUST (first's `in scope`)
        ELSE `the scope found in` id rest

-- Whether the section has the sub-provision with the given path, written as the text writes it: "(2)(b)".
GIVEN sectionId IS A STRING, path IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section has the sub-provision` MEANS `the path is listed in` sectionId path `the provision paths`

GIVEN sectionId IS A STRING, path IS A STRING, entries IS A LIST OF `Provision path`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the path is listed in` MEANS
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   first's `section` EQUALS sectionId AND first's `path` EQUALS path
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE `the path is listed in` sectionId path rest
